[center][size=6][b]LETHAL GARGOYLES[/b][/size]
[i]This mischievous gargoyle's goal is to follow you around and annoy you with his witty taunts. But be wary, he's not so passive if you don't respect his space![/i][/center]

[quote][b]I want to be transparent. Some content in "Lethal Gargoyles" was created using AI-assisted tools. I understand a lot of people don't wish to support anything that was made using AI, so this disclaimer is here in respect of those views.[/b][/quote]

[line]

[size=5][b]Mod Showcase[/b][/size]

[youtube]BGAoOVgEUk0[/youtube]

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Voiced Gargoyle[/b] - features the voice of the modder, with 160+ unique voice lines, and more to come.
[*][b]Dynamic Behavior[/b] - the gargoyle tries to stay close while remaining hidden, but will become aggressive if you get too close.
[*][b]Varied Taunts[/b] - a wide range of taunts for different situations, including general taunts, aggro responses, death reactions, and more.
[*][b]Customizable Voice Lines[/b] - add or replace voice lines with your own custom OGG files. Instructions below.
[*][b]Scrap Item[/b] - adds a Gargoyle Statue as scrap that can be interacted with to hear the Gargoyle's voice lines. Be careful, the Eyeless Dog can hear it too.
[*][b]Configuration Options[/b] - disable specific voice lines or adjust other settings through the mod's configuration file.
[/list]

[spoiler][b]Gargoyle Behavior (spoilers)[/b]
[list]
[*]The gargoyle's primary goal is to annoy the player. It will try to stay close while remaining hidden, but its stealth skills are still under development.
[*]If the player enters its aggro range, it will chase and attack them. Be careful, as it might occasionally push you into walls.
[*]If the target player is walking on a catwalk, the gargoyle will try to push the player, potentially off the catwalk.
[/list][/spoiler]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]BepInEx 5[/b] (5.4.2100)
[*][b]LethalLib[/b] by Evaisa
[*][b]PathfindingLib[/b] by Zaggy1024
[/list]

[b]This is a host and client mod. Everyone in the lobby needs it installed[/b], or the Gargoyle will not spawn correctly.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[b]With Vortex or Mod Organizer 2[/b] - hit the Mod Manager Download button and follow the installer. It will ask whether you want the Coroner compatibility file. Leave it ticked unless you have a reason not to.

[b]By hand[/b] - open the zip and drag the [b]BepInEx[/b] folder into your Lethal Company folder, the one with [b]Lethal Company.exe[/b] in it. If you also run Coroner, drag the [b]BepInEx[/b] folder out of [b]Optional\Coroner[/b] as well. There is a READ ME FIRST text file in the zip with the same steps.

Start the game once after installing. That is what writes the config file and creates your Custom Voice Lines folders.

[line]

[size=5][b]Add or Replace Voice Lines[/b][/size]

[spoiler][size=4][b]1. Audio format and location[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]All custom voice lines [b]must be in OGG format[/b]. MP3, WAV and the rest are not supported.
[*]Put your OGG files in the [b]Custom Voice Lines[/b] folder, which lives inside a [b]Lethal Gargoyles[/b] folder in your game directory. For example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Lethal Company\Lethal Gargoyles\Custom Voice Lines[/code]
[*]The mod creates that folder, and a subfolder for every category below, the first time it runs. Launch the game once with the mod installed and the folders will be waiting for you.
[*][b]Do not[/b] put custom voice lines in the "Voice Lines" folder. That one belongs to the mod and is overwritten on update.
[*]There is a maximum size of [b]500 KB[/b] per OGG file, because of a size limit on Steam network messages.
[/list]

[size=4][b]2. Voice line categories[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Combat Dialog
[*]Taunt - Activity
[*]Taunt - Aggro
[*]Taunt - Enemy
[*]Taunt - Gargoyle Death
[*]Taunt - General
[*]Taunt - Player Death
[*]Taunt - Prior Death
[*]Taunt - EmployeeClass (requires the Employee Classes mod)
[*]Taunt - SteamIDs
[/list]

[size=4][b]3. Naming conventions[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Hardcoded categories.[/b] For "Taunt - Activity", "Taunt - Enemy", "Taunt - Prior Death" and "Taunt - EmployeeClass", you can add multiple variations of the same taunt by taking the original file name as a base and adding a suffix. To add variations of taunt_priordeath_Abandoned, name your files taunt_priordeath_Abandoned2.ogg, taunt_priordeath_Abandoned_Custom.ogg and so on. The mod picks randomly between everything sharing that base name.
[*][b]Other categories.[/b] Any file name works. Drop it in the matching folder under Custom Voice Lines.
[/list]

[size=4][b]4. Disabling voice lines[/b][/size]

Any individual line, shipped or custom, can be switched off in the mod's config file.

[size=4][b]5. Steam ID taunts[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Name a file [b][SteamID][optional text].ogg[/b] and the Gargoyle will play it when that specific player is his target. For example 76561198012345678_ConorTaunt.ogg or 76561198012345678.ogg.
[*]There is a 2.5% chance he plays a Steam ID taunt, so they do not wear out.
[*]If a player has several, he picks one at random.
[/list][/spoiler]

[line]

